WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.700
Harley Quinn might still be relatively new
to DC Comics, but she's already gone through

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:06.819
some significant style shifts in the years
since her debut.

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:10.620
What moviegoers got to see of that character
in Suicide Squad was just a sliver of her

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.620
story.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.890
Here's a run-down of the most significant
moments in Harley's evolution.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.279
Batman: The Animated Series

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:21.949
In 1992, Harley Quinn made her debut as the
Joker's right-hand gal in Batman: The Animated

00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:22.949
Series.

00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:26.890
The character was inspired by a surreal harlequin
scene from Days of Our Lives, featuring actress

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.269
Arleen Sorkin, an old friend of writer and
producer Paul Dini.

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:34.780
When Dini saw the scene, he knew exactly who
he wanted as the Joker’s new sidekick.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.410
He recruited Sorkin herself to do the character's
voice.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.570
"But what about all our friends?

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:44.600
Ivy and Two Face and Hat Guy and Lizard Man
and Puppet Head and-"

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.790
Her original ensemble was designed by artist
Bruce Timm, and remains her most iconic costume.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.620
Early Appearances

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:56.300
Harley made her comic book debut in Batman
Adventures #12, maintaining much of the same

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.120
look as her animated appearance.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.050
As the details of her seduction by The Joker
became a focal point, specifically in Batman

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:06.530
Adventures: Mad Love, she started to show
a little more shape and a little more sass.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:11.420
In December 2000, she got her first comic
series, where she temporarily drops her relationship

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.939
with the Joker, choosing Poison Ivy instead.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:17.770
The new series made her more realistic, but
it still kept her costume the same for its

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:18.880
full run.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.530
Arkham Asylum

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:25.960
Harley's sex appeal made its first real appearance
in the 2009 video game Batman: Arkham Asylum,

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.310
making her barely recognizable.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:31.990
Her backstory remained similar, but her look
was sharply different: blonde pigtails, a

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.659
revealing corset, and thigh-high boots.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:36.680
She was also not as light-hearted as she'd
once been.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.740
Dini, who also wrote the game, defends her
controversial changes, saying, "I wanted to

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.390
make it clear that Harley Quinn was out of
her mind."

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.000
"Surprise!"

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:52.579
"Ya know bats I always thought there was spark
between us."

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:56.380
This new version of Harley would also appear
in the rest of the Arkham series, each time

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.409
appearing slightly different.

00:01:58.409 --> 00:01:59.409
The New 52

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:04.570
When DC rebooted the Suicide Squad comics
as part of its New 52 event, Harley got a

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:09.580
major style overhaul, introducing her red
and blue pigtails, corset, hot pants, and

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.580
heels.

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:14.390
The series also revamped her origin story
to include the chemical skin alterations later

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:16.090
seen in the cinematic version.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:20.220
Soon after that, her standalone series got
its own reboot, and ushered in the era of

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.790
blue and pink eyeshadow.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:25.520
Although the colors of her costume and hair
harkened back to her signature red-and-black,

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.540
her midriff, legs, and more were still on
full display.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.140
Suicide Squad

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:34.300
The cinematic Suicide Squad followed suit
in displaying Harley's allure onscreen.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:38.940
In the flick, Margot Robbie's Harley also
sported pigtails partially dyed blue and pink,

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:44.230
tiny shorts, a tattered t-shirt, red varsity
jacket, a ton of tattoos, and boots.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.890
While the get-up paid tribute to the past
versions of the character, it also arrived

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.210
as its own new spin.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:53.330
Bruce Timm, Harley’s original designer,
told Gizmodo that the character's new design

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:55.260
looked “really cool."

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:00.010
Dini, meanwhile, thought the Daddy's Monster
approach was a good way to make it work.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:05.470
"I know it's jarring for a lot of the people
who love the classic Bruce Tim suit, I love

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:09.790
it myself, I mean if in that world, I just
don't see it happening."

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:13.810
The changes have since been incorporated into
DC’s Rebirth initiative, launched in the

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:15.030
summer of 2016.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:19.400
This new Harley Quinn has the screen version's
hairstyle, makeup, and a much more urbanized

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.400
garment game.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.400
Phew!

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.480
Keeping up with all those style changes can
be, well...vexing.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.320
"I'm known to be quite vexing, I'm just forewarning
you."

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.320
Thanks for watching!

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.350
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.450
And leave us a comment to let us know which
is your favorite Harley Quinn costume…

